            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Sections partition the document into a content hierarchy. A section is an implicit enclosure. Each section begins with a title and ends at the next sibling section, ancestor section, or end of document. Nested section levels must be sequential."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A section title marks the beginning of a section and also acts as the heading for that section. The section title must be prefixed with a section marker, which indicates the section level. The number of equal signs in the marker represents the section level using a 0-based index (e.g., two equal signs represents level 1). A section marker can range from two to six equal signs and must be followed by a space."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the HTML output, the section title is represented by a heading tag. The number of the heading tag is one more than the section level (e.g., section level 1 becomes an h2 tag). The section level ranges from 0-5. This limit was established primarily due to the fact that HTML only provides heading tags from h1 to h6 (making level 5 the upper limit)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Document Title (Level 0)\n\n== Level 1 Section Title\n\n=== Level 2 Section Title\n\n==== Level 3 Section Title\n\n===== Level 4 Section Title\n\n====== Level 5 Section Title\n\n== Another Level 1 Section Title"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Section titles available in an article doctype"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The section titles are rendered as:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
